module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpChartCover.Cartier
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.CentreInsidePower
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Properties.ExtendFiniteType.IdealSheafOfHomComap
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Blowup.IdealFactorization

/-!
# The second centre on the charts of the blowup: globalizing the chart factorization

Let `X` be a scheme, `I` a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf on it with blowup `b : X' = Bl_I(X) ⟶ X`
and exceptional ideal `E = I·𝒪_{X'}`, and let `J ≤ I ^ d` be a second ideal sheaf on `X`. On the
standard affine chart `Spec Γ(X, U)[I/a]` of [Stacks, Tag 0804] the extension of `J` factors as
`aᵈ` times the *normalization* `J/aᵈ`, the ideal generated by the fractions `x/aᵈ` for
`x ∈ J(U)`; that is `affineBlowupAlgebra.map_ideal_eq_map_pow_mul_normalize`, a statement about
rings.

This file globalizes it. The charts cover the blowup, so an identity of ideal sheaves on `X'`
may be checked on them, and the result is a *criterion*: an ideal sheaf `Z'` on `X'` satisfies
`b⁻¹J·𝒪_{X'} = E ^ d · Z'` if and only if it is the normalization `J/aᵈ` on every chart. In
particular that factorization determines `Z'` uniquely, which is what identifies a `Z'` given by
some other construction — a `Proj` quotient, say — with the one obtained by dividing by the
effective Cartier divisor `E ^ d`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.map_chartΓIso_ideal_comap`: the inverse image of an ideal sheaf,
  read on the standard chart at `a`, is the extension of its ideal on `U`.
* `Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.map_chartΓIso_ideal_exceptionalIdeal_pow`: `E ^ d` is cut out by `aᵈ`
  on the standard chart at `a`.
* `Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.comap_eq_exceptionalIdeal_pow_mul_iff`: **the globalization.** For
  `J ≤ I ^ d`, the factorization `b⁻¹J·𝒪_{X'} = E ^ d · Z'` holds exactly when `Z'` is the
  normalization `J/aᵈ` on every standard chart.
* `Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.existsUnique_comap_eq_exceptionalIdeal_pow_mul`: for `J ≤ I ^ d` the
  second factor exists and is **unique**.
* `Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.comap_idealSheafDataOfHom_eq_exceptionalIdeal_pow_mul_iff`: the same
  criterion for a centre presented as the image of a quasi-coherent module `A` under a morphism
  `φ : A ⟶ 𝒪_X`, where the generators of `Z'` on the chart are the fractions `φ(x)/aᵈ`.

## Implementation notes

Everything is transported along `Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.chartΓIso`, the identification of
`Γ(X', W)` with `Γ(X, U)[I/a]` for `W` the chart's image, which is an isomorphism of rings and
so takes ideals to ideals injectively
(`Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_map_hom_injective`). The two sides of the factorization are computed
there by `Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE` together with
`Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.appLE_chartOpen`, which says that under `chartΓIso` the restriction map
`Γ(X, U) ⟶ Γ(X', W)` is the canonical map into the blowup algebra.

The forward direction of the criterion needs the second factor to be determined by the first,
which is cancellation of the principal ideal `(aᵈ)`: `a` maps to a nonzerodivisor of
`Γ(X, U)[I/a]` (`Stacks.Blowup.isRegular_algebraMap_affineBlowupAlgebra`, the ring-level half of
[Stacks, Tag 02OS (1)]), so does `aᵈ`, and
`Ideal.eq_of_span_singleton_mul_eq_span_singleton_mul` below cancels it. Mathlib's cancellation
`Ideal.span_singleton_mul_right_injective` assumes a domain, which the blowup algebra is not.

Existence of the second factor is not proved again here: it is
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_comap_eq_exceptionalIdeal_pow_mul`, division by the effective Cartier
divisor `E ^ d`. What this file adds to it is the chart description, and with it uniqueness.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached. The chart factorization occurs inside the proof of
[Stacks, Tag 080B] rather than as a statement of its own, and the clauses of 080B themselves are
in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/CompositeCentre.lean`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 080B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/080B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0804](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0804)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07Z3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07Z3)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerColimit

universe u

/-- **Cancelling a principal ideal generated by a nonzerodivisor.** If `s` is a nonzerodivisor
then `(s) · P = (s) · Q` forces `P = Q`. Unlike `Ideal.span_singleton_mul_right_injective` this
needs no domain hypothesis. -/
theorem Ideal.eq_of_span_singleton_mul_eq_span_singleton_mul {A : Type*} [CommRing A] {s : A}
    (hs : s ∈ nonZeroDivisors A) {P Q : Ideal A}
    (h : Ideal.span {s} * P = Ideal.span {s} * Q) : P = Q := by
  have key : ∀ P' Q' : Ideal A, Ideal.span {s} * P' ≤ Ideal.span {s} * Q' → P' ≤ Q' := by
    intro P' Q' hle p hp
    obtain ⟨q, hq, hpq⟩ := Ideal.span_singleton_mul_le_span_singleton_mul.mp hle p hp
    rwa [(mul_cancel_left_mem_nonZeroDivisors hs).mp hpq]
  exact le_antisymm (key _ _ h.le) (key _ _ h.ge)

/-- The generators of the normalization `J/aᵈ` of an ideal `J ⊆ Iᵈ`, named so that a rewrite
finds them: `affineBlowupAlgebra.normalize` is a `def`, for which no equation lemma applies. -/
theorem affineBlowupAlgebra.normalize_eq_span {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {S : Type*} [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] (I J : Ideal R) (a : R) [IsLocalization.Away a S] (d : ℕ) (hJ : J ≤ I ^ d) :
    affineBlowupAlgebra.normalize (S := S) I J a d hJ =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun x : ↥J ↦
        affineBlowupAlgebra.fraction (S := S) I a d ⟨(x : R), hJ x.2⟩) := rfl

namespace Stacks.BlowUpChartCover

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)

/-- The ideal of a product of ideal sheaves on an affine open, named so that a rewrite matches
it first-order: going through `Pi.mul_apply` exhausts the heartbeat budget here. -/
private theorem ideal_mul_apply {Y : Scheme.{u}} (K L : Y.IdealSheafData)
    (W : Y.affineOpens) : (K * L).ideal W = K.ideal W * L.ideal W := rfl

/-- An inclusion `J ≤ I ^ d` of ideal sheaves read on an affine open. -/
theorem ideal_le_ideal_pow {J : X.IdealSheafData} {d : ℕ} (hJ : J ≤ I ^ d)
    (U : X.affineOpens) : J.ideal U ≤ I.ideal U ^ d := hJ U

variable (U : X.affineOpens) (a : I.ideal U)

/-- The chart identification carries the generator of the exceptional ideal on the standard
chart at `a` to the image of `a` in the affine blowup algebra. -/
theorem chartΓIso_hom_chartGenerator :
    (chartΓIso I U a).hom (chartGenerator I U a) =
      algebraMap Γ(X, U.1) (chartRing I U a) (a : Γ(X, U.1)) := by
  have hcomp := DFunLike.congr_fun
    (congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom (appLE_chartOpen I U a)) (a : Γ(X, U.1))
  rwa [CommRingCat.hom_comp] at hcomp

/-- **The inverse image of an ideal sheaf on the standard chart at `a`.** Transported along
`chartΓIso` it is the extension of the ideal of `J` on `U` to the affine blowup algebra. -/
theorem map_chartΓIso_ideal_comap (J : X.IdealSheafData) :
    Ideal.map (chartΓIso I U a).hom.hom
        ((J.comap (blowUpToBase I)).ideal (chartOpen I U a)) =
      Ideal.map (algebraMap Γ(X, U.1) (chartRing I U a)) (J.ideal U) := by
  rw [Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE J (blowUpToBase I) U (chartOpen I U a)
      (chartOpen_le I U a), Ideal.map_map, ← CommRingCat.hom_comp, appLE_chartOpen,
    CommRingCat.hom_ofHom]

/-- **The `d`-th power of the exceptional ideal on the standard chart at `a`.** Transported
along `chartΓIso` it is generated by `aᵈ`. -/
theorem map_chartΓIso_ideal_exceptionalIdeal_pow (d : ℕ) :
    Ideal.map (chartΓIso I U a).hom.hom
        ((exceptionalIdeal I ^ d).ideal (chartOpen I U a)) =
      Ideal.span {algebraMap Γ(X, U.1) (chartRing I U a) (a : Γ(X, U.1)) ^ d} := by
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_pow, Pi.pow_apply,
    ideal_exceptionalIdeal_eq_span_chartGenerator I U a, Ideal.map_pow, Ideal.map_span,
    Set.image_singleton, chartΓIso_hom_chartGenerator I U a, Ideal.span_singleton_pow]

/-- The image of `a` in the affine blowup algebra of the standard chart at `a` is a
nonzerodivisor, and so is each of its powers. -/
theorem pow_algebraMap_mem_nonZeroDivisors (d : ℕ) :
    algebraMap Γ(X, U.1) (chartRing I U a) (a : Γ(X, U.1)) ^ d ∈
      nonZeroDivisors (chartRing I U a) :=
  Submonoid.pow_mem _ (isRegular_iff_mem_nonZeroDivisors.mp
    (Stacks.Blowup.isRegular_algebraMap_affineBlowupAlgebra (I.ideal U) (a : Γ(X, U.1))
      (Localization.Away (a : Γ(X, U.1))))) d

end Stacks.BlowUpChartCover

namespace Stacks.BlowUpChartCover

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)

/-- **The left-hand side of the factorization, read on the standard chart at `a`**: the
extension of `J` to the affine blowup algebra is `aᵈ` times the normalization `J/aᵈ`. This is
`affineBlowupAlgebra.map_ideal_eq_span_singleton_mul_normalize` transported along
`chartΓIso`. -/
theorem map_chartΓIso_ideal_comap_eq (J : X.IdealSheafData) (d : ℕ) (hJ : J ≤ I ^ d)
    (U : X.affineOpens) (a : I.ideal U) :
    Ideal.map (chartΓIso I U a).hom.hom
        ((J.comap (blowUpToBase I)).ideal (chartOpen I U a)) =
      Ideal.span {algebraMap Γ(X, U.1) (chartRing I U a) (a : Γ(X, U.1)) ^ d} *
        affineBlowupAlgebra.normalize (S := Localization.Away (a : Γ(X, U.1)))
          (I.ideal U) (J.ideal U) (a : Γ(X, U.1)) d (ideal_le_ideal_pow I hJ U) := by
  rw [map_chartΓIso_ideal_comap I U a J]
  exact affineBlowupAlgebra.map_ideal_eq_span_singleton_mul_normalize
    (S := Localization.Away (a : Γ(X, U.1))) (I.ideal U) (J.ideal U) (a : Γ(X, U.1)) d
    (ideal_le_ideal_pow I hJ U)

/-- The right-hand side of the factorization, read on the standard chart at `a`: the first
factor becomes the principal ideal `(aᵈ)`. -/
theorem map_chartΓIso_ideal_pow_mul (d : ℕ) (Z' : (blowUp I).IdealSheafData)
    (U : X.affineOpens) (a : I.ideal U) :
    Ideal.map (chartΓIso I U a).hom.hom
        ((exceptionalIdeal I ^ d * Z').ideal (chartOpen I U a)) =
      Ideal.span {algebraMap Γ(X, U.1) (chartRing I U a) (a : Γ(X, U.1)) ^ d} *
        Ideal.map (chartΓIso I U a).hom.hom (Z'.ideal (chartOpen I U a)) := by
  rw [ideal_mul_apply, Ideal.map_mul, map_chartΓIso_ideal_exceptionalIdeal_pow I U a d]

/-- The standard affine charts of the blowup cover it, as a family indexed by a pair of an
affine open of the base and a section of the centre there. -/
theorem iSup_chartOpen_eq_top :
    ⨆ i : Σ U : X.affineOpens, I.ideal U, (chartOpen I i.1 i.2).1 = ⊤ := by
  refine eq_top_iff.mpr fun x hx ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨U, hU⟩ := TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mp ((iSup_opensRange_chart_eq_top I).ge hx)
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mp hU
  exact TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨U, a⟩, ha⟩

/-- Two ideal sheaves on the blowup are equal once they agree on every standard chart, read
through `chartΓIso`. -/
private theorem ext_of_map_chartΓIso_ideal_eq {Z₁ Z₂ : (blowUp I).IdealSheafData}
    (h : ∀ (U : X.affineOpens) (a : I.ideal U),
      Ideal.map (chartΓIso I U a).hom.hom (Z₁.ideal (chartOpen I U a)) =
        Ideal.map (chartΓIso I U a).hom.hom (Z₂.ideal (chartOpen I U a))) :
    Z₁ = Z₂ :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext_of_iSup_eq_top
    (ι := Σ U : X.affineOpens, I.ideal U) (fun i ↦ chartOpen I i.1 i.2)
    (iSup_chartOpen_eq_top I) fun ⟨U, a⟩ ↦
      Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_map_hom_injective (chartΓIso I U a) (h U a)

/-- **The globalization of `affineBlowupAlgebra.map_ideal_eq_map_pow_mul_normalize`.** For a
second centre `J ≤ I ^ d` on `X`, an ideal sheaf `Z'` on the blowup satisfies
`b⁻¹J·𝒪_{X'} = E ^ d · Z'` if and only if, on every standard affine chart `Γ(X, U)[I/a]` of the
blowup, it is the normalization `J/aᵈ` — the ideal generated by the fractions `x/aᵈ` for
`x ∈ J(U)`. -/
theorem comap_eq_exceptionalIdeal_pow_mul_iff (J : X.IdealSheafData) (d : ℕ) (hJ : J ≤ I ^ d)
    (Z' : (blowUp I).IdealSheafData) :
    J.comap (blowUpToBase I) = exceptionalIdeal I ^ d * Z' ↔
      ∀ (U : X.affineOpens) (a : I.ideal U),
        Ideal.map (chartΓIso I U a).hom.hom (Z'.ideal (chartOpen I U a)) =
          affineBlowupAlgebra.normalize (S := Localization.Away (a : Γ(X, U.1)))
            (I.ideal U) (J.ideal U) (a : Γ(X, U.1)) d (ideal_le_ideal_pow I hJ U) := by
  constructor
  · intro heq U a
    have hW := map_chartΓIso_ideal_comap_eq I J d hJ U a
    rw [heq, map_chartΓIso_ideal_pow_mul I d Z' U a] at hW
    exact Ideal.eq_of_span_singleton_mul_eq_span_singleton_mul
      (pow_algebraMap_mem_nonZeroDivisors I U a d) hW
  · intro hchart
    refine ext_of_map_chartΓIso_ideal_eq I fun U a ↦ ?_
    rw [map_chartΓIso_ideal_comap_eq I J d hJ U a, map_chartΓIso_ideal_pow_mul I d Z' U a,
      hchart U a]

/-- **The second factor of the inverse image of a centre inside a power is unique.** For
`J ≤ I ^ d` there is exactly one ideal sheaf `Z'` on the blowup of `X` in `I` with
`b⁻¹J·𝒪_{X'} = E ^ d · Z'`. Existence is division by the effective Cartier divisor `E ^ d`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_comap_eq_exceptionalIdeal_pow_mul`); uniqueness is the chart
description, which determines `Z'` on a cover of the blowup. -/
theorem existsUnique_comap_eq_exceptionalIdeal_pow_mul (J : X.IdealSheafData) (d : ℕ)
    (hJ : J ≤ I ^ d) :
    ∃! Z' : (blowUp I).IdealSheafData,
      J.comap (blowUpToBase I) = exceptionalIdeal I ^ d * Z' := by
  obtain ⟨Z', hZ'⟩ := AlgebraicGeometry.exists_comap_eq_exceptionalIdeal_pow_mul I J d hJ
  refine ⟨Z', hZ', fun W hW ↦ ?_⟩
  have h1 := (comap_eq_exceptionalIdeal_pow_mul_iff I J d hJ W).mp hW
  have h2 := (comap_eq_exceptionalIdeal_pow_mul_iff I J d hJ Z').mp hZ'
  exact ext_of_map_chartΓIso_ideal_eq I fun U a ↦ (h1 U a).trans (h2 U a).symm

/-! ### A centre presented as the image of a quasi-coherent module -/

variable {A : X.Modules} [A.IsQuasicoherent] (φ : A ⟶ structureModule X)

/-- A value of `φ` over an affine open lies in the image ideal sheaf there. -/
theorem structureAppₗ_mem_idealSheafDataOfHom (U : X.affineOpens) (x : Γ(A, U.1)) :
    structureAppₗ φ U.1 x ∈ (idealSheafDataOfHom A φ).ideal U :=
  LinearMap.mem_range_self _ x

/-- The normalization of the image of `φ` is generated by the fractions `φ(x)/aᵈ`: the elements
of the image ideal on `U` are exactly the values of `φ` there. -/
theorem normalize_idealSheafDataOfHom (d : ℕ) (hJ : idealSheafDataOfHom A φ ≤ I ^ d)
    (U : X.affineOpens) (a : I.ideal U) :
    affineBlowupAlgebra.normalize (S := Localization.Away (a : Γ(X, U.1)))
        (I.ideal U) ((idealSheafDataOfHom A φ).ideal U) (a : Γ(X, U.1)) d
        (ideal_le_ideal_pow I hJ U) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun x : Γ(A, U.1) ↦
        affineBlowupAlgebra.fraction (S := Localization.Away (a : Γ(X, U.1)))
          (I.ideal U) (a : Γ(X, U.1)) d
          ⟨structureAppₗ φ U.1 x,
            ideal_le_ideal_pow I hJ U (structureAppₗ_mem_idealSheafDataOfHom φ U x)⟩) := by
  rw [affineBlowupAlgebra.normalize_eq_span]
  congr 1
  refine Set.ext fun z ↦ ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · rintro ⟨y, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ : ∃ x : Γ(A, U.1), structureAppₗ φ U.1 x = (y : Γ(X, U.1)) := y.2
    refine ⟨x, ?_⟩
    have hsub : (⟨structureAppₗ φ U.1 x,
          ideal_le_ideal_pow I hJ U (structureAppₗ_mem_idealSheafDataOfHom φ U x)⟩ :
        ↥(I.ideal U ^ d)) = ⟨(y : Γ(X, U.1)), ideal_le_ideal_pow I hJ U y.2⟩ := Subtype.ext hx
    exact congrArg (affineBlowupAlgebra.fraction (S := Localization.Away (a : Γ(X, U.1)))
      (I.ideal U) (a : Γ(X, U.1)) d) hsub
  · rintro ⟨x, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨⟨structureAppₗ φ U.1 x, structureAppₗ_mem_idealSheafDataOfHom φ U x⟩, rfl⟩

/-- **The factorization of a module-presented centre on the blowup.** Let `A` be a
quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module and `φ : A ⟶ 𝒪_X` a morphism whose image ideal sheaf `J` lies in
`I ^ d`. An ideal sheaf `Z'` on the blowup satisfies `b⁻¹J·𝒪_{X'} = E ^ d · Z'` if and only if,
on every standard affine chart `Γ(X, U)[I/a]`, it is generated by the fractions `φ(x)/aᵈ` for
`x` a section of `A` over `U`. -/
theorem comap_idealSheafDataOfHom_eq_exceptionalIdeal_pow_mul_iff (d : ℕ)
    (hJ : idealSheafDataOfHom A φ ≤ I ^ d) (Z' : (blowUp I).IdealSheafData) :
    (idealSheafDataOfHom A φ).comap (blowUpToBase I) = exceptionalIdeal I ^ d * Z' ↔
      ∀ (U : X.affineOpens) (a : I.ideal U),
        Ideal.map (chartΓIso I U a).hom.hom (Z'.ideal (chartOpen I U a)) =
          Ideal.span (Set.range fun x : Γ(A, U.1) ↦
            affineBlowupAlgebra.fraction (S := Localization.Away (a : Γ(X, U.1)))
              (I.ideal U) (a : Γ(X, U.1)) d
              ⟨structureAppₗ φ U.1 x,
                ideal_le_ideal_pow I hJ U
                  (structureAppₗ_mem_idealSheafDataOfHom φ U x)⟩) := by
  rw [comap_eq_exceptionalIdeal_pow_mul_iff I (idealSheafDataOfHom A φ) d hJ Z']
  exact forall_congr' fun U ↦ forall_congr' fun a ↦ by
    rw [normalize_idealSheafDataOfHom I φ d hJ U a]

end Stacks.BlowUpChartCover

end
